WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.925
What breaks in production,
and what guards against it?

2
00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:07.694
No support plan, and nothing is read:
the error surfaces, the runbook's

3
00:00:07.694 --> 00:00:12.975
pre-flight calls the API first, and the
Health Dashboard is the interim path.

4
00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:17.329
The full-access policy attached for
convenience lets the reader write,

5
00:00:17.329 --> 00:00:19.100
so the kit uses three actions.

6
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.320
A GovCloud account read from
the commercial endpoint fails,

7
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.475
so the partition names the region
and the caller is checked.

8
00:00:25.475 --> 00:00:29.300
Eleven identifiers in one call
are refused before calling.

9
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.557
A retirement without AWS's flag
could stop an instance on its date,

10
00:00:33.557 --> 00:00:36.238
so the kit's rule makes
it action required.

11
00:00:36.238 --> 00:00:39.832
And in GovCloud, EventBridge
won't bring public events,

12
00:00:39.832 --> 00:00:41.810
so the kit reads on a schedule.
